.TH GLPI 8 "August 2025" "GLPI 10.0.19" "System Administrator's Manual"
.SH NAME
glpi \- Install and configure GLPI on Alpine Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glpi
.SH DESCRIPTION
GLPI (Free IT Asset Management) is a web application for IT asset management and helpdesk. This package installs GLPI into \fI/var/www/glpi\fR and prepares the environment required for its operation on Alpine Linux.

.SH INSTALLATION
Installing the GLPI package performs the following actions:
.IP \[bu] 2
Creates required directories (\fI/var/www/glpi\fR, \fI/var/lib/glpi\fR).
.IP \[bu]
Installs the GLPI application files.
.IP \[bu]
Deploys the \fIglpi-console\fR script to \fI/usr/bin\fR.
.IP \[bu]
Sets permissions to allow GLPI to write to the \fIfiles\fR, \fIconfig\fR, \fIplugins\fR, and \fImarketplace\fR directories.
.IP \[bu]
Removes the web installer script \fIinstall.php\fR for security reasons.

.SH CONFIGURATION
After installation, configure your web server (Apache or Nginx) and PHP-FPM using the configuration files provided in the \fIglpi-apache2\fR, \fIglpi-nginx\fR, and \fIglpi-fpm\fR subpackages.

Then, access GLPI through your web browser to complete the setup via the web interface.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/var/www/glpi\fR
Main GLPI application directory.
.TP
\fI/usr/bin/glpi-console\fR
GLPI CLI console.
.TP
\fI/etc/apache2/conf.d/glpi-apache2.conf\fR
Apache2 configuration for GLPI.
.TP
\fI/etc/nginx/http.d/glpi-nginx.conf\fR
Nginx configuration for GLPI.
.TP
\fI/etc/php84/conf.d/glpi-fpm.ini\fR
PHP-FPM configuration for GLPI.

